<title>FRANCE: ALPINE SKIING-KNAUSS WINS MEN'S SUPER-G.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-KNAUSS WINS MEN'S SUPER-G.</headline>
<dateline>VAL D'ISERE, France 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Hans Knauss won a men's World Cup Alpine skiing super-G on Monday in an unofficial time of one minute 23.26 seconds.</p>
<p>Guenther Mader of Austria was second in 1:23.29 and Steve Locher of Switzerland third in 1:23.42.</p>
</text>
